# The one integer value shape, as every module that carries a copy spells it. @PREFIX@ is the
# module's prefix and @ONTOLOGY@ its ontology IRI; nothing else varies. The master is
# bddo:IntegerValueShape; the copies exist because shapes are validated module by module (the
# family contracts and the engine load one module's shapes), and a sh:node into another module's
# graph is silently satisfied when that module is not loaded. integer-value-shape.json lists the
# modules that carry a copy, for a gate that asserts each equals this template.
@PREFIX@:IntegerValueShape a sh:NodeShape ; rdfs:label "Integer value shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <@ONTOLOGY@> ;
    sh:message "An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte)." ;
    sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:positiveInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] [ sh:datatype xsd:int ] [ sh:datatype xsd:long ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedInt ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedLong ] [ sh:datatype xsd:short ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedShort ] [ sh:datatype xsd:byte ] [ sh:datatype xsd:unsignedByte ] ) .
